A stratification 
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{X}=\mathcal{X}' \sqcup \mathcal{S}_1 \sqcup \cdots \sqcup \mathcal{S}_N
\end{align*}
is called \textit{$\Theta$-stratification} if each 
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{S}_i \subset \mathcal{X}' \sqcup \mathcal{S}_1 \sqcup \cdots \sqcup \mathcal{S}_i
\end{align*}
is a $\Theta$-stratum (in particular $\mathcal{X}'\subset \mathcal{X}$ is open).

A \textit{$G$-Higgs bundle} consists of 
\begin{align*}
    (\mathcal{E}, \theta), \ \mathcal{E} \to C, \ \theta \in \Gamma((\mathcal{E}\times^G \mathfrak{g})\otimes \Omega_C)
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{E} \to C$ is a $G$-bundle and $G$ acts on $\mathfrak g$ via the adjoint representation.

It is a zero-shifted symplectic stack~\cite{PTVV}; indeed we have 
\begin{align*}
    \mathrm{Higgs}_G=\Omega_{\mathrm{Bun}_G}
\end{align*}
where $\mathrm{Bun}_G$ is the moduli stack of $G$-bundles, and $\Omega_{\mathrm{Bun}_G}$ denotes the cotangent stack of $\mathrm{Bun}_G$.

We denote by 
\begin{align}\label{univ:F}
    (\mathcal{F}, \vartheta), \ \mathcal{F} \to C \times \mathrm{Higgs}_{\operatorname{GL}_r}
\end{align}
the universal Higgs bundle.

