\label{lem:PLGm}
Let $\nu \colon B\mathbb{G}_m \to \mathcal{H}_b$ be a map corresponding to 
\begin{align*}
    \mathrm{pt}\mapsto M=M_1 \oplus \cdots \oplus M_k
\end{align*}
for $M_i \in \operatorname{Coh}^{\heartsuit}(\mathcal{C}_b)$ 
with scheme theoretic support $C_i=\mathrm{Supp}(M_i)$ (which is regarded as an effective divisor on $S$) and 
$\mathbb{G}_m$-weight $(\nu_1, \ldots, \nu_k)$. 
Then the $\mathbb{G}_m$-weight of $\nu^* \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{L}}$ is given by 
\begin{align*}
    \mathrm{wt}(\nu^* \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{L}})=\sum_{i=1}^k l_i \cdot \nu_i.
\end{align*}
Here $l_i:=\deg_{C_i}(\mathcal{L}|_{C_i})\in \mathbb{Z}$ is defined as in (\ref{deg:Cb}).

By (\ref{def:Psharp}), we have 
\begin{align*}
  \nu^* \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{L}}=\bigotimes_{i=1}^k \left(\det \chi(\mathcal{L}\otimes M_i)\otimes \det \chi(M_i)^{-1}\right) \otimes \det \chi(\mathcal{L})^{-1}\otimes \det \chi(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{C}_b}).
\end{align*}
Then the lemma follows since the $\mathbb{G}_m$-weight of $M_i$ is $\nu_i$ 
and 
\begin{align*}
    \chi(\mathcal{L}\otimes M_i)-\chi(M_i)=\chi(\mathcal{L}|_{C_i})-\chi(\mathcal{O}_{C_i})
\end{align*}
which is $\deg_{C_i}(\mathcal{L}|_{C_i})$.

